  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039, scVI n200 + ViT-L + multi-profile + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250) combines all individually superior design choices. The remaining uncertainty is whether an alternative RNA encoder could interact differently with the strong ViT-L image signal in the multimodal setting. config_051 isolates this by changing only the RNA encoder from scVI to scGPT while holding every other component at its empirically best value (ViT-L, multi-profile, transformer, weighted). In RNA-only, scGPT underperformed scVI (0.514 vs 0.653), but the large multimodal lift (+0.072 from RNA-only to multimodal with ViT-L) suggests the image branch may partially compensate for a weaker RNA representation, or scGPT's learned biological structure could be complementary in a way PCA is not. As the final experiment, this single-variable test either confirms scVI as the optimal RNA encoder in the best multimodal configuration or reveals a surprising interaction that could set a new best. It is the highest-information, lowest-risk choice remaining."
